-- title:
--   Proposition 6.12 — Azuma and Freedman bounds for $I_t-\sum_{\tau\le t}\rho_\tau$ and for the cumulative reward
-- statement:
--   Run Algorithm 4 on any finite grids $\mathcal B^\circ,\mathcal A^\circ\subseteq[0,1]$ (Definition 6.4), with radii $\psi_t$ that are $\mathcal F_t$-measurable, in the probability model of Sec. 3. Let
--   $$
--   \rho_\tau=\mathbb E\big[\mathbb I(V^{\mathrm{sell}}_\tau\le B_\tau)-\mathbb I(V^{\mathrm{buy}}_\tau\ge A_\tau)\,\big|\,\mathcal F_{\tau-1}\big],\qquad \sigma_\tau^2=\mathrm{Var}\big[\mathbb I(V^{\mathrm{sell}}_\tau\le B_\tau)-\mathbb I(V^{\mathrm{buy}}_\tau\ge A_\tau)\,\big|\,\mathcal F_{\tau-1}\big].
--   $$
--   For every $T\in\mathbb N$ and $\delta\in(0,1)$:
--
--   1. with probability at least $1-\delta$, simultaneously for every $t=1,\dots,T$,
--   $$\Big|I_t-\sum_{\tau=1}^t\rho_\tau\Big|\le\sqrt{2T\log(2/\delta)};$$
--   2. for every deterministic $v\ge0$, with probability at least $1-\delta$, simultaneously for every $t\le T$ such that $\sum_{\tau=1}^t\sigma_\tau^2\le v$,
--   $$\Big|I_t-\sum_{\tau=1}^t\rho_\tau\Big|\le\sqrt{2v\log(2/\delta)}+\frac43\log(2/\delta);$$
--   3. and 4. the same two statements hold for the cumulative reward $\sum_{\tau\le t}r_\tau$, with $\rho_\tau$ and $\sigma^2_\tau$ replaced by the conditional mean $\mathbb E[r_\tau\mid\mathcal F_{\tau-1}]$ and the conditional variance $\mathrm{Var}[r_\tau\mid\mathcal F_{\tau-1}]$.
--
--   These concentration bounds reduce the control of the imbalance and of the revenue to the control of their conditional drifts.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: Algorithm 4 with the radii of Notation 6.9 (such that (16) holds with probability at least 1 − δ) → Algorithm 4 with any finite grids B°, A° ⊆ [0, 1] (Definition 6.4), any F_t-measurable radii and any probability law V on ℝ²; reason: the proof uses only that the increments lie in [−1, 1] (every posted price is in [0, 1]) and are adapted; the paper's configurations are instances
--   - reading: F_t contains all valuations and algorithmic random draws through round t (pp. 42, 47) → F_t = σ(W_1, …, W_t) with W_s = ((V^sell_s, V^buy_s), U_s); F_0 trivial; reason: this is the σ-algebra the sentence describes
--   - encoding: ρ_τ, σ²_τ and the conditional mean and variance of r_τ → Mathlib's condExp and condVar given F_{τ−1}; reason: these are defined up to null sets, which does not change the probability of the events
--   - encoding: T rounds with (V^sell_t, V^buy_t) i.i.d. from V and the Bernoulli draws X ∼ Bern(p), Y ∼ Bern(p) of Algorithm 4 → measurable sequences indexed by ℕ whose round vectors ((V^sell_t, V^buy_t), U_t) are mutually independent with law V ⊗ Unif[0,1]; a draw Bern(p) is 1{U_t < p}; index 0 and indices beyond T are unused; reason: given the past, 1{U_t < p} has law Bern(p); at most one draw is made per round; every event involves rounds 1, …, T only
--   - reading: Algorithm 5 has no return statement after its second loop (Line 26) → it then returns the outer pair (b_0, a_{M−1}); reason: the paper leaves this case undefined; the outer pair keeps the active sets nested, and on grids with a pair b < a and nonnegative radii it is never reached (Proposition 6.11)
--   - reading: Line 23 of Algorithm 4 updates F̂_t, Ŝ_t on the active sets only → F̂_t(b) = (1/t) Σ_{τ≤t} χ^sell_τ(b) and Ŝ_t(a) = (1/t) Σ_{τ≤t} χ^buy_τ(a) for every price, with F̂_0 = Ŝ_0 = 0; reason: Algorithm 5 evaluates the bounds only on the active sets, which are nested, so the values the algorithm uses are the same
--   - encoding: log → Real.log, the natural logarithm; reason: the DKW and Azuma exponents are base e
-- source:
--   Maran, Restelli, Stradi, No-Regret Revenue Maximization in Sequential Market Making Under Inventory Constraints, arXiv:2610.24562v1, Proposition 6.12, p. 42

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_InvMarketMaking_LOB_IsRoundModel
import Definitions.Def_InvMarketMaking_LOB_lobRound

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace InvMarketMaking.LOB

/-- **Proposition 6.12** (Maran, Restelli, Stradi, arXiv:2610.24562v1, p. 42). Let
`ρ_τ = E[I(V^sell_τ ≤ B_τ) − I(V^buy_τ ≥ A_τ) | ℱ_{τ−1}]` and
`σ²_τ = Var[I(V^sell_τ ≤ B_τ) − I(V^buy_τ ≥ A_τ) | ℱ_{τ−1}]`, with `ℱ_t` generated by all
valuations and algorithmic random draws through round `t`. For every `δ ∈ (0,1)`:
1. with probability at least `1 − δ`, simultaneously for every `t = 1, …, T`,
   `|I_t − Σ_{τ=1}^t ρ_τ| ≤ √(2T log(2/δ))`;
2. for every deterministic `v ≥ 0`, with probability at least `1 − δ`, simultaneously for every
   `t ≤ T` such that `Σ_{τ=1}^t σ²_τ ≤ v`, `|I_t − Σ_{τ=1}^t ρ_τ| ≤ √(2v log(2/δ)) + (4/3) log(2/δ)`;
3. and 4. the same two conclusions for the cumulative reward `Σ_{τ ≤ t} r_τ`, with `ρ_τ` and `σ²_τ`
   replaced by the conditional mean and variance of `r_τ` given `ℱ_{τ−1}`.

**Formalization Note** Stated for Algorithm 4 with any finite grids `B°, A° ⊆ [0,1]` (Definition 6.4,
p. 34; this keeps every posted price in `[0,1]`, so `r_t ∈ [−1, 1]`) and any radii adapted to `(ℱ_t)`
(Notation 6.9: the radius of time `t` depends only on quantities generated by the end of round
`t`). The probability model is `IsRoundModel`; `log` is the natural logarithm. The conditional
expectation and variance are Mathlib's `condExp` and `condVar` with respect to `roundSigma M (τ−1)`. -/
theorem proposition_6_12 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (V : Measure (ℝ × ℝ)) [IsProbabilityMeasure V] (M : Market Ω) (hM : IsRoundModel P V M)
    (C : LOBConfig Ω) (hB : ↑C.Bg ⊆ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) (hA : ↑C.Ag ⊆ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1)
    (hψF : ∀ t x, Measurable[roundSigma M t] (C.ψF t x))
    (hψS : ∀ t x, Measurable[roundSigma M t] (C.ψS t x))
    (T : ℕ) (δ : ℝ) (hδ : δ ∈ Set.Ioo 0 1) :
    (ENNReal.ofReal (1 - δ) ≤ P {ω | ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T,
      |imbalance C M t ω - ∑ τ ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t,
          (P[invIncrement C M τ | roundSigma M (τ - 1)]) ω| ≤
        Real.sqrt (2 * T * Real.log (2 / δ))}) ∧
    (∀ v : ℝ, 0 ≤ v → ENNReal.ofReal (1 - δ) ≤ P {ω | ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T,
      ∑ τ ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t, Var[invIncrement C M τ; P | roundSigma M (τ - 1)] ω ≤ v →
      |imbalance C M t ω - ∑ τ ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t,
          (P[invIncrement C M τ | roundSigma M (τ - 1)]) ω| ≤
        Real.sqrt (2 * v * Real.log (2 / δ)) + 4 / 3 * Real.log (2 / δ)}) ∧
    (ENNReal.ofReal (1 - δ) ≤ P {ω | ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T,
      |∑ τ ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t, reward C M τ ω - ∑ τ ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t,
          (P[reward C M τ | roundSigma M (τ - 1)]) ω| ≤
        Real.sqrt (2 * T * Real.log (2 / δ))}) ∧
    (∀ v : ℝ, 0 ≤ v → ENNReal.ofReal (1 - δ) ≤ P {ω | ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T,
      ∑ τ ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t, Var[reward C M τ; P | roundSigma M (τ - 1)] ω ≤ v →
      |∑ τ ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t, reward C M τ ω - ∑ τ ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t,
          (P[reward C M τ | roundSigma M (τ - 1)]) ω| ≤
        Real.sqrt (2 * v * Real.log (2 / δ)) + 4 / 3 * Real.log (2 / δ)}) := by sorry

end InvMarketMaking.LOB
